# #1637 (EigenScript#1647): an UNCAUGHT bool raise -- the AOT dies with the
# VM's text, line and exit code after the same stdout. The comparison result
# is a bool held in a compiled function's local, and `== 1` on it (the old
# 1/0 idiom the issue migrates) raises rather than quietly answering false.
define ready(n) as:
    local ok is n > 2
    print of ok
    if ok == 1:
        return "migrated?"
    return "unreachable"
print of "before"
print of (ready of 5)
print of "after"
